# The exact denial admission-public-https-drops-a-private-range.yaml must
# produce. One document, one reason: the signature-verification egress rule
# refusing an exclusion set that is one range short.
#
# admission-install-network-bypasses.expected already names this same message,
# which is precisely why that fixture cannot stand in for this one: its
# shortened-exclusion document ALSO carries the shared `part-of` selector
# instead of the admission-controller component, so it stays denied for the
# selector when the exclusion comparison is removed, its message set never
# changes, and the removal survives. Here the message IS the exclusion
# comparison: this document is the reviewed shape in every other respect.
NetworkPolicy kyverno/kyverno-public-https widens its exact reviewed admission flow
